testability: PASSIVE

[HYP] box CORS static whitelist + wildcard enables cross-origin exfiltration
class: MISCONFIG
asset: box.signageos.io/ and /login/
confidence: 55
reasoning: 17 static ACAO values including `http://box.signageos.io` (plaintext HTTP) and `https://*.zdusercontent.com` (wildcard). Static whitelist — spoofed Origin NOT reflected. No `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials` on any box path. The wildcard + HTTP variant expand trust boundary but without credentials flag, browser-based credential theft is blocked.
evidence_needed: Confirm no ACAO+ACAC combination under any Origin; demonstrate that the wildcard is the only theoretically exploitable combination
verify_steps: `curl -sI -H "Origin: https://evil.test" https://box.signageos.io/ 2>&1 | grep -iE 'access-control'` + `curl -sI -H "Origin: https://evil.zdusercontent.com" https://box.signageos.io/ 2>&1 | grep -iE 'access-control'`
impact: Limited — no credentials flag means no cookie/auth theft. The HTTP variant (`http://box.signageos.io`) is the most notable but requires MITM on plaintext. Low-medium severity.
testability: PASSIVE

